      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cash developed as an unincorporated community in the 1870s around a railroad depot on the Cheraw and Darlington Railroad line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cash_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was originally named Cash's Depot after Colonel Ellerbe Boggan Crawford Cash, a prominent local planter and lawyer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cash_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office called Cash's Depot served the community from 1880 until it closed in 1917.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cash%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cash is located in the Sandhills region, which is characterized by gently rolling terrain and sandy, well-drained soils.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cash_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The landscape around Cash is dominated by undulating dunes and sand sheets formed by ancient wind processes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cash_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Cash experiences a humid subtropical climate with hot, muggy summers and annual rainfall exceeding 45 inches.",
